      "text": "The Deerwood Auditorium, built in 1935 as a Works Progress Administration project, is a rare surviving example of federal relief architecture in Minnesota.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deerwood%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The historic auditorium’s exterior was recently renovated, preserving its original look while making the building available for events.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cityofdeerwood.gov/about-deerwood"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town grew when the Northern Pacific Railroad expanded from Carlton to Brainerd, and today a park sits on the old Deerwood Railroad Depot site.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cityofdeerwood.gov/about-deerwood"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Deerwood earned its name from the plentiful deer roaming the surrounding woods.",
